# Python bytecode. Two .pyc files were tracked before this file existed, one of
# them the compiled form of lib/typefloor.py -- so the repository carried a
# stale copy of the module whose whole defect had been that it reported a
# verdict the compiler never produced. Bytecode is a build product of whichever
# interpreter happens to run; it does not belong in version control.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
